-- title:
--   Dichotomy at p‖N: unit Uₚ after extension, or residual local irreducibility
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing $p$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, $\mathfrak m$-adically complete, with finite residue field) of characteristic zero in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal, and let $\chi \colon \mathbb{T}_S \to \mathcal{O}'$ be a ring homomorphism, where $\mathbb{T}_S =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Assume $p \mid N$ but $p^2 \nmid N$. Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $\mathcal{O}'$, i.e. a free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho \colon \operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) \to \operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}'} V$ that is adically continuous (for each $n$ there is a finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise acts trivially on $V$ modulo $\mathfrak m^n$). Assume the Eichler–Shimura relations: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. The conclusion is a disjunction. Either there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}''$ of the same kind (domain, adically complete, finite residue field, characteristic zero) with $p$ in its maximal ideal, a ring homomorphism $\iota \colon \mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi' \colon \mathbb{T}_{S \setminus \{p\}} \to \mathcal{O}''$ on the larger Hecke algebra obtained by allowing $U_p$ among the generators, such that $\chi'$ restricted along the inclusion $\mathbb{T}_S \subseteq \mathbb{T}_{S \setminus \{p\}}$ equals $\iota \circ \chi$ and $\chi'(U_p)$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}''$; or, for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a nonunit, every submodule $L$ of the residual representation $\operatorname{ResidueField}(\mathcal{O}') \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} V$ stable under $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ is $\bot$ or $\top$.
--
--   This is the dichotomy used at a prime exactly dividing the level: either the Hecke eigensystem becomes $p$-ordinary in the sense that $U_p$ takes a unit value after a finite enlargement of the coefficient ring, or the residual representation is irreducible on a decomposition group at $p$. It reflects the local shape at $p \| N$ of the automorphic representation (special or supercuspidal at $p$), and feeds the ordinarity input to the deformation-theoretic datum: it is cited in establishing the ordinarity condition for the Hecke–Galois datum and in the construction of a module-finite discrete valuation ring over which the point has unit $U_p$-value.
-- source:
